#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Introduction to Absolute and Relative Frequency]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Imagine rolling a die multiple times 🎲]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- How often does each number appear?]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- This is where absolute and relative frequency come in!]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Let's start by imagining a simple situation: rolling a die multiple times. How often does each number appear? This is where the concepts of absolute and relative frequency come in!")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Absolute frequency tells us the number of times each number appears when we roll the die.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Relative frequency, on the other hand, is the ratio of the absolute frequency to the total number of rolls.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Absolute Frequency]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Definition: Number of times an event occurs 📊]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Rolling a die 10 times]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- If we roll a 3 three times, the absolute frequency of 3 is 3]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Absolute frequency is simply the number of times an event occurs. For example, if we roll a die 10 times, and we get a 3 three times, the absolute frequency of rolling a 3 is 3.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Let's consider an example: Rolling a die 10 times.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("If we roll a 3 three times, the absolute frequency of 3 is 3.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Relative Frequency]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Definition: Ratio of absolute frequency to total trials 📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Formula: $ "Relative Frequency" = ("Absolute Frequency") / ("Total Trials") $]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Example: Rolling a die 10 times, 3 threes → $ "Relative Frequency" = 3 / 10 = 0.3 $]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Relative frequency is the ratio of the absolute frequency to the total number of trials. It tells us how often an event occurs relative to the total number of trials.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("The formula for relative frequency is the absolute frequency divided by the total number of trials.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("For example, if we roll a die 10 times and get a 3 three times, the relative frequency of rolling a 3 is 3 divided by 10, which is 0.3.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Summary]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Absolute frequency: Number of times an event occurs 📊]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Relative frequency: Ratio of absolute frequency to total trials 📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Example: Rolling a die 10 times, 3 threes → Absolute: 3, Relative: 0.3]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To summarize, absolute frequency is the number of times an event occurs.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Relative frequency is the ratio of the absolute frequency to the total number of trials.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("For example, if we roll a die 10 times and get a 3 three times, the absolute frequency of rolling a 3 is 3, and the relative frequency is 0.3.")
]
]